{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01044",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.29,
      "end_seconds": 4.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting, come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 5.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.27,
      "end_seconds": 13.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.29,
      "end_seconds": 28.37,
      "duration_seconds": 13.08,
      "text": "I wanted to get sudden hearing loss in one ear looked at. I'm not great at remembering details, uh, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.33,
      "end_seconds": 33.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.09,
      "end_seconds": 37.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "It's been about four days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.26,
      "end_seconds": 39.16,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.03,
      "end_seconds": 45.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 46.02,
      "end_seconds": 52.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.7,
      "end_seconds": 56.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Any ringing as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.67,
      "end_seconds": 60.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Yes, since last weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.51,
      "end_seconds": 65.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.85,
      "end_seconds": 73.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.62,
      "end_seconds": 80.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.93,
      "end_seconds": 88.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.3,
      "end_seconds": 93.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Any discharge or ear pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.35,
      "end_seconds": 105.82,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "No, no discharge, no ear pain. I did have a blocked feeling at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.42,
      "end_seconds": 108.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Did you notice any dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.0,
      "end_seconds": 112.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 113.71,
      "end_seconds": 119.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice dizziness. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.22,
      "end_seconds": 126.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.13,
      "end_seconds": 136.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, did you notice any facial weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.86,
      "end_seconds": 140.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "No facial weakness, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.15,
      "end_seconds": 144.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Right, how's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.17,
      "end_seconds": 147.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.07,
      "end_seconds": 151.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.84,
      "end_seconds": 156.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Uh, no, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.53,
      "end_seconds": 159.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.75,
      "end_seconds": 168.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.97,
      "end_seconds": 172.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Alright, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.02,
      "end_seconds": 187.54,
      "duration_seconds": 13.52,
      "text": "For the anxiety, I believe. My daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I take allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 189.37,
      "end_seconds": 197.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.2,
      "end_seconds": 202.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.82,
      "end_seconds": 207.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.33,
      "end_seconds": 211.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.78,
      "end_seconds": 215.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.53,
      "end_seconds": 218.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.9,
      "end_seconds": 224.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.73,
      "end_seconds": 227.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.24,
      "end_seconds": 233.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.78,
      "end_seconds": 235.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.02,
      "end_seconds": 240.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.37,
      "end_seconds": 245.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Right, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.35,
      "end_seconds": 248.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.51,
      "end_seconds": 268.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.81,
      "end_seconds": 283.11,
      "duration_seconds": 12.3,
      "text": "I've had anxiety for five years now. I just want to get back to normal, really. I've had gout for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.96,
      "end_seconds": 286.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.47,
      "end_seconds": 288.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "I have asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 300.1,
      "end_seconds": 309.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.29,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 36.5 degrees, respiratory rate 16, pulse 84, BP is 113 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.03,
      "end_seconds": 311.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.07,
      "end_seconds": 318.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.78,
      "end_seconds": 322.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.26,
      "end_seconds": 339.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "The ear drum looks normal and the tuning fork is heard louder in the other ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.34,
      "end_seconds": 367.14,
      "duration_seconds": 22.8,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Let me tell you where I've got to. The most likely explanation is sudden hearing loss needing urgent treatment. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a wax or fluid blockage, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.74,
      "end_seconds": 371.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.96,
      "end_seconds": 393.64,
      "duration_seconds": 20.68,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's sudden hearing loss needing urgent treatment, and we'll know more once the an MRI scan is back. So, to recap quickly. You've had sudden hearing loss in one ear for about four days, and no discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.17,
      "end_seconds": 395.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.13,
      "end_seconds": 402.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an MRI scan for sudden hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.89,
      "end_seconds": 404.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.41,
      "end_seconds": 435.68,
      "duration_seconds": 29.27,
      "text": "Let's book an urgent hearing test to look into sudden hearing loss. For this, prednisolone, 60 milligrams, once a day, seven days. It's for sudden hearing loss. This is time-critical, so I'm starting treatment today. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'll also refer you to the ENT team. Let's plan a check in one week. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.53,
      "end_seconds": 441.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}